<HEAD><style>/* Story Map — page vocabulary. Paint rides native attrs; classes carry shape, rhythm, and the
   two named ornaments (rounded tint panel, think-aloud tail). */
.gml-card {
  --code-character: var(--palette-1);
  --code-setting: var(--palette-2);
  --code-problem: var(--palette-3);
  --code-resolution: var(--palette-4);
}

/* 1 · Story-element code: rounded solid tag + coded panel with a dot tab */
.tag .gml-label[data-variant='solid'] { border-radius: 999pt; --label-pad-inline: 14pt; --label-pad-block: 8pt; }
.coded.gml-grid-cell { position: relative; --cell-radius: 16pt; }
.coded.gml-grid-cell::after {
  content: ""; position: absolute; top: 16pt; right: 16pt; width: 16pt; height: 16pt;
  border-radius: 50%; background: var(--dot, var(--code-character));
}
.code-character { --dot: var(--code-character); }
.code-setting { --dot: var(--code-setting); }
.code-problem { --dot: var(--code-problem); }
.code-resolution { --dot: var(--code-resolution); }

/* 2 · Rounded tint panel (ornament 1) — flat, no outline, no shadow */
.panel.gml-grid-cell { --cell-radius: 16pt; --cell-border-width: 0; --cell-shadow: none; }

/* 3 · Illustration plate: one cutout at real scale inside a tint panel, or a scene clipped to the radius */
.plate.gml-grid-cell { --cell-radius: 16pt; --cell-shadow: none; }
.plate .gml-figure__img { object-fit: contain; }
.plate-scene { --figure-radius: 16pt; }
.plate-scene .gml-figure__img { border-radius: 16pt; }




/* 3d · Clue panel: air between the picture and its caption block */
.clue .gml-figure { margin-block-end: 14pt; }

/* 3c · Character disc: an equal round tint disc behind each cutout in a cast row; name and line hug their disc */
.disc .gml-figure { background: var(--surface-color); border-radius: 50%; padding: 18pt; }
.disc.gml-grid-cell > .gml-grid-cell__content { --heading-gap-above: calc(10 * var(--rhythm-unit, 1pt)); --subheading-gap-below: calc(6 * var(--rhythm-unit, 1pt)); }

/* 3b · Scene copy: the template's tint panel carried onto a full-bleed painting so the type reads on any skin */
.scene-copy.gml-grid-cell { --cell-radius: 16pt; border-radius: 16pt; }

/* 3e · Story-map links: ink arrows between coded cells trace the reading path */
.link.gml-grid-cell { --cell-icon-size: 40pt; color: var(--palette-ink); }

/* 4 · Reading column: storybook measure with paragraph air */
.prose .gml-paragraph { text-wrap: pretty; }

/* 5 · Think-aloud bubble (ornament 2): oat panel with one tail toward the speaker */
.think.gml-grid-cell { position: relative; --cell-radius: 18pt; --cell-shadow: none; }
.think.gml-grid-cell::after {
  content: ""; position: absolute; right: -11pt; top: 56pt; width: 24pt; height: 24pt;
  background: var(--surface-color); transform: rotate(45deg); border-radius: 3pt;
}

/* 6 · Numeral chip: ink circle, white Baloo numeral; empty variant for write-in ordering */
.chip { --marker-bg: var(--palette-ink); --marker-color: var(--card-color); --marker-size: 38pt; --marker-font-size: 23pt; --marker-font-weight: 800; }
.chip-empty { --marker-bg: var(--card-color); --marker-color: transparent; --marker-border-color: var(--palette-ink); --marker-border-width: 3pt; --marker-size: 42pt; }

/* 7 · Coded field divider: the solid field runs to the trim, never a rounded panel */
.field .gml-grid-cell { --cell-radius: 0; border-radius: 0; }

/* 8 · Takeaway beside the plot, with its source line */
.note .gml-paragraph { text-wrap: balance; }
.metric { font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums; }
.tag.gml-label-group { margin-block-end: 18pt; }

/* 9 · Ledger table: compact insets so five projected-size rows fit one card */
.ledger.gml-table { --table-cell-padding: 7pt 18pt; }</style></HEAD>
<section image-layout="blank" id="mGB0UaNhP-" card-margin-hidden="true"><img src="https://cdn-staging.gamma.app/QWjS6fBfpt/generated-images/bvmkQZpvbIIQZSkMmWBGN.png" saved-media-id="n8sfwye7ae0ttm7" source="image.ai-generated" background="true" image-style="gouache-scene" alt="Matte gouache painting of the wide grassy plains of southern Brazil, a winding earth track crossing rolling grassland with a small distant cattle herd, warm naturalistic marigold, leaf green, brick red and sky blue notes, visible soft brushstrokes, quiet warm cream sky across the upper-left half, no people, no buildings, no flags, no text or lettering" meta="{&quot;width&quot;:1920,&quot;height&quot;:1088}"><grid spacing="none"><grid-item id="H0w7tM8hya" padding="68pt 68pt 52pt"><grid spacing="none" vertical-sizing="hug"><grid-item id="Zp3K67WllU" class="panel scene-copy" background-overlay="tint" background-overlay-color="surface" background-overlay-intensity="0.9" padding="26pt 32pt 30pt" colspan="40"><display size="md">The War of<br>the Rags</display><p>A ten-year revolt about taxes, distance and who got to make the rules.</p><labels class="tag"><label variant="solid">Brazil · 1835–1845</label></labels></grid-item><spacer mode="fill"></spacer></grid><spacer mode="fill"></spacer></grid-item></grid><notes><p>Introduce the surprising English name: the Ragamuffin War. Reassure the audience that this story focuses on ideas, journeys and ingenious boats rather than violent battles.</p></notes></section>
<section image-layout="blank" id="qIaY_uqGSB"><grid spacing="none"><grid-item id="7fw-XKW-Ql"><h2>Brazil's cattle corner</h2><grid spacing="large" vertical-sizing="fill"><grid-item id="6w1nwj2Lgy" class="prose" colspan="26"><p font-size="23pt">Rio Grande do Sul sits at Brazil's southern tip, beside Uruguay and Argentina.</p><p font-size="23pt">Its grassy plains held huge cattle herds and cowboys called <b>gaúchos</b>. Rio de Janeiro was about <b>2,000 km</b> away.</p></grid-item><grid-item id="nrXup3SEwg" vertical-align="center" colspan="34"><custom-code>
<style>
  .rag-map { height: 10em; font-family: var(--body-font); color: var(--body-color); }
  .rag-map svg { width: 100%; height: 100%; display: block; }
  .rag-map .land { fill: var(--surface-color); stroke: var(--body-color); stroke-width: 3; }
  .rag-map .south { fill: var(--palette-2); stroke: var(--body-color); stroke-width: 2; }
  .rag-map .route { stroke: var(--palette-3); stroke-width: 3; stroke-dasharray: 8 8; fill: none; }
  .rag-map .pin { fill: var(--palette-3); stroke: var(--card-color); stroke-width: 3; }
  .rag-map text { font-family: var(--body-font); fill: var(--body-color); font-size: 18px; font-weight: 700; }
  .rag-map .small { font-size: 15px; font-weight: 400; }
</style>
<div class="rag-map">
  <svg width="600" height="330" viewBox="0 0 600 330" role="img" aria-label="Simple map of Brazil showing Rio Grande do Sul in the south and Rio de Janeiro far to the north">
    <path class="land" d="M268 18 L332 46 L377 42 L420 78 L451 112 L431 148 L456 181 L425 208 L405 244 L372 283 L341 318 L316 280 L301 235 L270 205 L251 163 L220 136 L236 96 L211 64 Z"></path>
    <path class="south" d="M316 280 L341 318 L372 283 L352 257 L328 254 Z"></path>
    <path class="route" d="M350 280 C380 246 397 210 410 166"></path>
    <circle class="pin" cx="410" cy="166" r="9"></circle>
    <text x="427" y="160">Rio de Janeiro</text>
    <text class="small" x="427" y="182">about 2,000 km away</text>
    <text x="206" y="309">Rio Grande do Sul</text>
    <text class="small" x="231" y="53">Brazil</text>
  </svg>
</div>
</custom-code></grid-item></grid></grid-item></grid><notes><p>Point to the long distance on the map. A journey to the capital could take weeks by horse. Source: <a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ragamuffin_War">Ragamuffin War overview</a>.</p></notes></section>
<section image-layout="blank" id="J9A9YGNMCi"><grid spacing="none"><grid-item id="U2ydQPoa7a"><grid spacing="large" vertical-sizing="hug"><grid-item id="-ZIL1Vwmm6" padding="30pt 54pt 26pt" colspan="28"><h2>It started with beef jerky</h2></grid-item><grid-item id="EwEQUEgLiB" padding="30pt 54pt 26pt" colspan="32"><p><b>Charque</b> was salt-dried beef that kept for months—the south’s biggest product.</p></grid-item></grid><grid marker="icon" marker-size="small" marker-position="inline" spacing="medium" vertical-sizing="hug"><grid-item id="WG1CeLaX3P" class="panel" background-color="palette-5" cell-style="solid" padding="14pt" colspan="20"><grid-item-label><icon src="https://iconscdn.pictographic.ai/image/BwTe3g4TpYJfFuYKdrdcv8.svg?stroke=45" source="image.pictographic.icon" alt="strip of salted dried meat"></icon></grid-item-label><p font-size="sm"><b>Southern charque:</b> The government taxed it heavily.</p></grid-item><grid-item id="yeFA8QhDwp" class="panel" background-color="palette-7" cell-style="solid" padding="14pt" colspan="20"><grid-item-label><icon src="https://iconscdn.pictographic.ai/image/oYwlUkHPv2ZwBwQHe4Jt.svg?stroke=45" source="image.pictographic.icon" alt="wooden scoop filled with salt crystals"></icon></grid-item-label><p font-size="sm"><b>Salt:</b> Even the salt needed to make it was taxed.</p></grid-item><grid-item id="gDgcuAxpDe" class="panel" background-color="palette-8" cell-style="solid" padding="14pt" colspan="20"><grid-item-label><icon src="https://iconscdn.pictographic.ai/image/4KJS77hmQiHI2Ldpx5rE.svg?stroke=45" source="image.pictographic.icon" alt="single round coin"></icon></grid-item-label><p font-size="sm"><b>Cheaper imports:</b> Charque from Uruguay and Argentina was barely taxed.</p></grid-item></grid></grid-item></grid><notes><p>Ask which product a shopper would choose if two looked similar but one cost less. Sources: <a href="https://brasilescola.uol.com.br/guerras/guerra-dos-farrapos.htm">Brasil Escola</a> and <a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ragamuffin_War">Ragamuffin War overview</a>.</p></notes></section>
<section image-layout="blank" id="sPJudVuNuw"><grid spacing="none"><grid-item id="HZdEN1gZFu"><h2>Who was making the rules?</h2><p>Emperor Pedro II was only nine. Grown-up <b>regents</b> ruled for him from the far-off capital.</p><spacer mode="fill"></spacer><grid spacing="small" vertical-sizing="hug"><grid-item id="VhgrxYC74L" class="panel" background-color="palette-5" vertical-align="center" cell-style="solid" padding="16pt" colspan="20"><grid spacing="small" vertical-sizing="hug" style="--cell-icon-size: 34pt;"><grid-item id="zSJ6xqrt39" align="center" vertical-align="center" colspan="12"><icon src="https://iconscdn.pictographic.ai/image/q9JE9zgWNwvW7GhBro6A.svg?stroke=45" source="image.pictographic.icon" alt="small crown on oversized throne"></icon></grid-item><grid-item id="htEa9VPzmD" vertical-align="center" colspan="48"><h4 font-size="22pt" align="left">Nine-year-old emperor</h4><p font-size="18pt" align="left">Pedro II wore the crown.</p></grid-item></grid></grid-item><grid-item id="r7AHu3e8uv" class="panel" background-color="surface" vertical-align="center" cell-style="solid" padding="16pt" colspan="20"><grid spacing="small" vertical-sizing="hug" style="--cell-icon-size: 34pt;"><grid-item id="4X2o7vdsF-" align="center" vertical-align="center" colspan="12"><icon src="https://iconscdn.pictographic.ai/image/xo4JFjiDSlQp1cplsQVT.svg?stroke=45" source="image.pictographic.icon" alt="government officials making rules"></icon></grid-item><grid-item id="FqNsJjDmhi" vertical-align="center" colspan="48"><h4 font-size="22pt" align="left">Regents ruled</h4><p font-size="18pt" align="left">They collected taxes from Rio de Janeiro.</p></grid-item></grid></grid-item><grid-item id="xIeZXf7k3K" class="panel" background-color="palette-6" vertical-align="center" cell-style="solid" padding="16pt" colspan="20"><grid spacing="small" vertical-sizing="hug" style="--cell-icon-size: 34pt;"><grid-item id="eHq3343uj7" align="center" vertical-align="center" colspan="12"><icon src="https://iconscdn.pictographic.ai/image/5SfBYQfhuwEpnROFgQ7S.svg?stroke=45" source="image.pictographic.icon" alt="map region choosing local rules"></icon></grid-item><grid-item id="HOfSt2auSr" vertical-align="center" colspan="48"><h4 font-size="22pt" align="left">The south objected</h4><p font-size="18pt" align="left">Ranchers wanted provinces to decide more for themselves.</p></grid-item></grid></grid-item></grid><spacer mode="fill"></spacer></grid-item></grid><notes><p>Explain that a regent rules while a monarch is too young. Source: <a href="https://www.encyclopedia.com/humanities/encyclopedias-almanacs-transcripts-and-maps/farroupilha-revolt">Encyclopedia.com</a>.</p></notes></section>
<section image-layout="blank" id="-_mzsLPLVS"><grid spacing="none"><grid-item id="82OaMDHuV4" padding-bottom="24pt"><h2 font-size="36pt">A rude nickname they kept</h2><p font-size="22pt"><i>Farrapo</i> means “rag” in Portuguese. Enemies used it to mock the rebels' fringed leather clothes.</p><grid marker="number" marker-size="small" marker-style="subtle" marker-shape="chevron" marker-position="above" marker-align="center" marker-fill="true" spacing="none" vertical-sizing="hug" padding="6pt 14pt 8pt" style="--marker-chip-padding: 0.28em; --marker-font-size: 22pt;"><grid-item id="2csfnwb6zL"><h4 font-size="24pt">Farrapo</h4><p font-size="18pt">A taunt from their enemies.</p></grid-item><grid-item id="Tf4a-CbYU_"><h4 font-size="24pt">Farrapos</h4><p font-size="18pt">The rebels kept the name proudly.</p></grid-item><grid-item id="DIX39r7mpo"><h4 font-size="24pt">Ragamuffins</h4><p font-size="18pt">The name used in English.</p></grid-item></grid><p font-size="20pt"><b>They turned an insult into a team name.</b></p></grid-item></grid><notes><p>Invite the audience to say the Portuguese word aloud: farrapo. Sources: <a href="https://www.encyclopedia.com/humanities/encyclopedias-almanacs-transcripts-and-maps/farroupilha-revolt">Encyclopedia.com</a> and <a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ragamuffin_War">Ragamuffin War overview</a>.</p></notes></section>
<section image-layout="blank" id="U-19IkxVJs"><grid spacing="none"><grid-item id="A14ufCf-p_"><h2>20 September 1835: the day it began</h2><grid spacing="medium" vertical-sizing="fill"><grid-item id="sZ5YEDZAMA" class="panel" background-color="palette-5" vertical-align="center" cell-style="solid" padding="20pt 22pt" colspan="23"><display size="md" font-size="42pt">20<br>September<br>1835</display><p font-size="18pt">Bento Gonçalves led rebel horsemen into Porto Alegre.</p></grid-item><grid-item id="aj8aoXZnib" colspan="37"><grid spacing="medium" vertical-sizing="hug"><grid-item id="mgxBL8WTOz" class="panel" background-color="surface" cell-style="solid" padding="14pt 18pt" colspan="30"><h4 font-size="22pt">They took the city</h4><p font-size="18pt">The revolt had begun.</p></grid-item><grid-item id="GekeY2nJ4Z" class="panel" background-color="palette-8" cell-style="solid" padding="14pt 18pt" colspan="30"><h4 font-size="22pt">The empire returned</h4><p font-size="18pt">Nine months later, it retook Porto Alegre and held the coast.</p></grid-item><grid-item id="03KUk0yDZB" class="panel" background-color="palette-6" cell-style="solid" padding="14pt 18pt" colspan="60"><h4 font-size="22pt">The rebels moved inland</h4><p font-size="18pt">The wide grasslands became their home ground.</p></grid-item></grid></grid-item></grid></grid-item></grid><notes><p>Emphasize the change in geography: the empire controlled the coast, while the Ragamuffins relied on inland plains. Sources: <a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ragamuffin_War">Ragamuffin War overview</a> and <a href="https://www.encyclopedia.com/humanities/encyclopedias-almanacs-transcripts-and-maps/farroupilha-revolt">Encyclopedia.com</a>.</p></notes></section>
<section image-layout="blank" id="aLu_7Dvjy9"><grid spacing="none"><grid-item id="WADdSuWZVo"><h2>They invented their own country</h2><grid spacing="large"><grid-item id="Aitl6bcyhs" class="prose" colspan="24"><p font-size="18pt">After winning at Seival, the rebels declared the <b>Riograndense Republic</b> on <b>11 September 1836</b>.</p><p font-size="18pt">Bento Gonçalves became its first president.</p><aside icon="false"><p font-size="18pt"><i>Liberty, Equality, Humanity</i></p></aside></grid-item><grid-item id="nckYre3Ve3" vertical-align="center" colspan="36"><custom-code><style>.republic-map { width: 100%; height: 260pt; font-family: var(--body-font); color: var(--body-color); } .republic-map svg { width: 100%; height: 100%; display: block; } .republic-map .land { fill: var(--surface-color); stroke: var(--body-color); stroke-width: 3; } .republic-map .republic { fill: var(--palette-6); stroke: var(--palette-2); stroke-width: 5; } .republic-map .pole { stroke: var(--body-color); stroke-width: 4; } .republic-map .flag { fill: var(--palette-3); } .republic-map text { font-family: var(--body-font); fill: var(--body-color); font-size: 18px; font-weight: 700; } .republic-map .small { font-size: 15px; font-weight: 400; }</style><div class="republic-map"><svg width="600" height="330" viewBox="0 0 600 330" role="img" aria-label="Simple map of Brazil with the Riograndense Republic outlined in the far south"><path class="land" d="M268 18 L332 46 L377 42 L420 78 L451 112 L431 148 L456 181 L425 208 L405 244 L372 283 L341 318 L316 280 L301 235 L270 205 L251 163 L220 136 L236 96 L211 64 Z"></path><path class="republic" d="M316 280 L341 318 L372 283 L352 257 L328 254 Z"></path><line class="pole" x1="369" y1="218" x2="369" y2="276"></line><path class="flag" d="M369 220 L421 233 L369 247 Z"></path><text x="392" y="285">Riograndense Republic</text><text class="small" x="392" y="306">declared inside Brazil</text><text class="small" x="238" y="59">Brazil</text></svg></div></custom-code></grid-item></grid></grid-item></grid><notes><p>A republic is a country without a monarch as its ruler. Sources: <a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ragamuffin_War">Ragamuffin War overview</a>, <a href="https://www.encyclopedia.com/humanities/encyclopedias-almanacs-transcripts-and-maps/farroupilha-revolt">Encyclopedia.com</a> and <a href="https://www.digitaleiro.com.br/sem-categoria/a-audacia-farroupilha-e-os-maiores-carros-de-boi-da-historia-usados-para-levar-os-veleiros-na-tomada-de-laguna/">Digitaleiro</a>.</p></notes></section>
<section image-layout="blank" id="A3oJAIXsdD"><grid spacing="none"><grid-item id="sD23Z2KGCu"><h2>Ten years, six moments</h2><spacer mode="fill"></spacer><grid marker="number" marker-size="large" marker-style="solid" marker-shape="rounded" marker-position="inline" marker-numbering-format="decimal" spacing="medium" vertical-sizing="hug" style="--marker-inline-size: 30pt; --marker-gap: 10pt;"><grid-item id="Bn_qTJoBdr" cell-style="subtle" padding="14pt" style="--marker-bg: #E9A23B; --marker-color: #2B2118;" colspan="20"><h4 font-size="20pt">1835</h4><p font-size="16pt">Rebels take Porto Alegre.</p></grid-item><grid-item id="-EyHttM0aB" cell-style="subtle" padding="14pt" style="--marker-bg: #3A7640; --marker-color: #FFFFFF;" colspan="20"><h4 font-size="20pt">1836</h4><p font-size="16pt">A new republic is declared.</p></grid-item><grid-item id="l5v--UxIBj" cell-style="subtle" padding="14pt" style="--marker-bg: #B8452B; --marker-color: #FFFFFF;" colspan="20"><h4 font-size="20pt">1837</h4><p font-size="16pt">Bento escapes prison and returns.</p></grid-item><grid-item id="oEauS5MvDW" cell-style="subtle" padding="14pt" style="--marker-bg: #2F6FB0; --marker-color: #FFFFFF;" colspan="20"><h4 font-size="20pt">1839</h4><p font-size="16pt">Boats cross land; the Juliana Republic is born.</p></grid-item><grid-item id="jVyroo8XPf" cell-style="subtle" padding="14pt" style="--marker-bg: #E9A23B; --marker-color: #2B2118;" colspan="20"><h4 font-size="20pt">1842</h4><p font-size="16pt">The Baron of Caxias arrives.</p></grid-item><grid-item id="T7I2ezFA7D" cell-style="subtle" padding="14pt" style="--marker-bg: #3A7640; --marker-color: #FFFFFF;" colspan="20"><h4 font-size="20pt">1845</h4><p font-size="16pt">Peace at Ponche Verde.</p></grid-item></grid><spacer mode="fill"></spacer></grid-item></grid><notes><p>Trace the timeline from left to right. Sources: <a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ragamuffin_War">Ragamuffin War overview</a> and <a href="https://pt.wikipedia.org/wiki/Seival">Seival</a>.</p></notes></section>
<section image-layout="blank" id="5x_Gxbb1rO"><grid spacing="none"><grid-item id="AdAOShHOYx"><h2>Meet the Ragamuffins</h2><spacer mode="fill"></spacer><grid marker="icon" marker-size="large" marker-style="subtle" marker-shape="circle" marker-position="above" marker-align="center" spacing="small"><grid-item id="czTxBSj_oe" align="center" cell-style="subtle" padding="16pt 10pt" colspan="12"><grid-item-label><icon src="https://iconscdn.pictographic.ai/image/3Pnb7xkSQUizAzDXSsmZUa.svg?stroke=45" source="image.pictographic.icon" alt="friendly cattle rancher leader portrait" meta="{&quot;description&quot;:&quot;A black cow's head silhouette, simplified into basic shapes, set against a clean white background, conveying the concept of cattle.&quot;}"></icon></grid-item-label><h4 font-size="19pt">Bento Gonçalves</h4><p font-size="14pt">Rancher, president and prison escaper.</p></grid-item><grid-item id="ExWzmJqQKo" align="center" cell-style="subtle" padding="16pt 10pt" colspan="12"><grid-item-label><icon src="https://iconscdn.pictographic.ai/image/EMr3BGEsQ4wygaZCNUwv.svg?stroke=45" source="image.pictographic.icon" alt="friendly Italian sailor portrait" meta="{&quot;description&quot;:&quot;An anchor symbolizing a sailor, conveying navigation and maritime profession.&quot;}"></icon></grid-item-label><h4 font-size="19pt">Giuseppe Garibaldi</h4><p font-size="14pt">Ran the rebel navy.</p></grid-item><grid-item id="KtHuLL4t_p" align="center" cell-style="subtle" padding="16pt 10pt" colspan="12"><grid-item-label><icon src="https://iconscdn.pictographic.ai/image/G9zXQk4mGc8sYami5ENN.svg?stroke=45" source="image.pictographic.icon" alt="friendly Brazilian woman rider and sailor portrait" meta="{&quot;description&quot;:&quot;An anchor symbol in a minimalist black and white design, signifying a sailor or nautical theme through the use of an anchor, a traditional sailor's emblem.&quot;}"></icon></grid-item-label><h4 font-size="19pt">Anita Garibaldi</h4><p font-size="14pt">Rode and sailed beside Giuseppe.</p></grid-item><grid-item id="k0WJO_00Sk" align="center" cell-style="subtle" padding="16pt 10pt" colspan="12"><grid-item-label><icon src="https://iconscdn.pictographic.ai/image/l0tQKkVtp6fJxMW0ukCL.svg?stroke=45" source="image.pictographic.icon" alt="friendly general announcing a proclamation portrait" meta="{&quot;description&quot;:&quot;A black silhouette of a person's head and shoulders, centered against a white background, symbolizing the concept of portrait.&quot;}"></icon></grid-item-label><h4 font-size="19pt">Antônio de Sousa Neto</h4><p font-size="14pt">Announced the new republic.</p></grid-item><grid-item id="Kl0uXkZBKM" align="center" cell-style="subtle" padding="16pt 10pt" colspan="12"><grid-item-label><icon src="https://iconscdn.pictographic.ai/image/xxw0M7xTP2k5Ua1G8PRe.svg?stroke=45" source="image.pictographic.icon" alt="friendly expedition commander portrait" meta="{&quot;description&quot;:&quot;A minimalist compass silhouette, often used as a symbol for exploration, navigation, and adventure, embodying the concept of an expedition.&quot;}"></icon></grid-item-label><h4 font-size="19pt">David Canabarro</h4><p font-size="14pt">Led the march on Laguna.</p></grid-item></grid><spacer mode="fill"></spacer></grid-item></grid><notes><p>Garibaldi later became famous in Italy, but his South American adventures came first. Sources: <a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ragamuffin_War">Ragamuffin War overview</a>, <a href="https://www.encyclopedia.com/humanities/encyclopedias-almanacs-transcripts-and-maps/farroupilha-revolt">Encyclopedia.com</a> and <a href="https://pt.wikipedia.org/wiki/Seival">Seival</a>.</p></notes></section>
<section image-layout="blank" id="e1DhczJ7UT" card-margin-hidden="true"><img src="https://cdn-staging.gamma.app/QWjS6fBfpt/generated-images/m9K_JMhDk4WzQrSCgrahO.png" saved-media-id="4wvvw6zl6sys5ve" source="image.ai-generated" background="true" image-style="gouache-scene" alt="Matte gouache storybook painting of a small nineteenth-century sailing boat lashed securely atop a giant wooden wheeled carriage, pulled across broad green grassland by a very long line of oxen, sandy marsh patches and distant lagoon water, no people, warm marigold, leaf green, brick red and sky blue notes, visible soft brushstrokes, the right third left as quiet warm cream sky and pale grass, no text or lettering" meta="{&quot;width&quot;:1920,&quot;height&quot;:1088}"><grid spacing="none"><grid-item id="SjPgg_iy8n" padding="48pt"><grid spacing="none" vertical-sizing="fill"><spacer span="30"></spacer><grid-item id="rSfER-dgx3" class="panel scene-copy" background-overlay="tint" background-overlay-color="surface" background-overlay-intensity="0.92" padding="20pt 24pt" colspan="30"><labels class="tag"><label variant="solid">1839</label></labels><h2 font-size="28pt">The time they put boats on wheels</h2><p font-size="18pt">Garibaldi lifted two boats onto giant wooden carriages.</p><p font-size="18pt">Around <b>100 oxen per boat</b> pulled them about <b>100 km</b> in <b>six days</b>.</p><p font-size="18pt">They splashed back into water at Tramandaí. The empire never noticed.</p></grid-item></grid></grid-item></grid><notes><p>The boats escaped a lagoon watched by imperial warships. Source: <a href="http://www.pampalivre.info/revolucao_farroupilha_a_epopeia_dos_lanchoes_pelos_campos_gauchos.htm">Pampa Livre</a>.</p></notes></section>
<section image-layout="blank" id="4yTo8yNRM2"><grid spacing="none"><grid-item id="nPtqst45mf"><h2>A second republic, for four months</h2><grid spacing="medium"><grid-item id="c69lACMWM4" class="panel" background-color="palette-8" align="center" vertical-align="center" cell-style="solid" padding="18pt" colspan="30"><display size="md" font-size="60pt">4</display><h3 font-size="24pt">about four months</h3></grid-item><grid-item id="3RbyV-iqha" class="panel" background-color="palette-6" cell-style="solid" padding="18pt" colspan="30"><h4 font-size="24pt">22 July 1839</h4><p font-size="18pt">The Ragamuffins captured the port of Laguna.</p></grid-item><grid-item id="UwiR4XGII1" class="panel" background-color="palette-5" cell-style="solid" padding="18pt" colspan="30"><h4 font-size="24pt">The Juliana Republic</h4><p font-size="18pt">They declared a second republic in the neighbouring province.</p></grid-item><grid-item id="FHf2gPINAr" class="panel" background-color="palette-7" cell-style="solid" padding="18pt" colspan="30"><h4 font-size="24pt">The empire returned</h4><p font-size="18pt">It retook the port. One boat had sunk in a storm; Garibaldi swam out alive.</p></grid-item></grid></grid-item></grid><notes><p>The daring boat journey worked, but the new republic was brief. Sources: <a href="https://www.digitaleiro.com.br/sem-categoria/a-audacia-farroupilha-e-os-maiores-carros-de-boi-da-historia-usados-para-levar-os-veleiros-na-tomada-de-laguna/">Digitaleiro</a>, <a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ragamuffin_War">Ragamuffin War overview</a> and <a href="https://pt.wikipedia.org/wiki/Farroupilha_II">Farroupilha II</a>.</p></notes></section>
<section image-layout="blank" id="RUqsmXEhlb"><grid spacing="none"><grid-item id="XXXa2vFZzJ"><h2 font-size="34pt">A promise that was broken</h2><p font-size="18pt">The <b>Black Lancers</b> were units of freed and formerly enslaved men, formed from 1836.</p><grid spacing="medium" vertical-sizing="hug"><grid-item id="t3xHQj7b8b" class="panel" background-color="palette-5" cell-style="solid" padding="16pt 18pt" colspan="30"><labels class="tag"><label variant="solid">The promise</label></labels><h3 font-size="24pt">Freedom for fighting</h3><p font-size="18pt">Some men were promised their freedom in exchange for serving as soldiers.</p></grid-item><grid-item id="83chjsMOF0" class="panel coded code-problem" background-color="palette-7" cell-style="solid" padding="16pt 18pt" colspan="30"><labels class="tag"><label variant="solid">What happened</label></labels><h3 font-size="24pt">The promise was not kept</h3><p font-size="18pt">The republic's 1843 constitution kept slavery. Most rebel leaders enslaved people themselves. Many Lancers never received freedom.</p></grid-item></grid></grid-item></grid><notes><p>This part should be read plainly. The Ragamuffins were not an anti-slavery movement. Source: <a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ragamuffin_War">Ragamuffin War overview</a>.</p></notes></section>
<section image-layout="blank" id="MLSKd7_xUR"><grid spacing="none"><grid-item id="bgm8ddeAZn" padding="68pt 18pt 68pt 68pt" colspan="22"><labels class="tag"><label variant="solid">1 March 1845</label></labels><h2 font-size="34pt">How it ended: a deal, not a battle</h2><p font-size="18pt">The <b>Treaty of Ponche Verde</b> ended the war with an agreement.<br><br><b>They gave up their country, but won the argument they had started over.</b></p></grid-item><grid-item id="uLb4F1AfMx" padding="68pt 68pt 68pt 18pt" colspan="38"><grid marker="icon" marker-size="small" marker-position="inline" spacing="medium" style="--marker-inline-size: 34pt; --marker-gap: 10pt;"><grid-item id="bHopicGJHz" class="panel" background-color="palette-5" cell-style="solid" padding="12pt" colspan="30"><grid-item-label><icon src="https://iconscdn.pictographic.ai/image/6VA9avqrIHp5TdMuc4V4.svg?stroke=45" source="image.pictographic.icon" alt="open hands pardon agreement"></icon></grid-item-label><h4 font-size="24pt">Pardons</h4><p font-size="17pt">Everyone was pardoned.</p></grid-item><grid-item id="sMTWRoGv0l" class="panel" background-color="palette-6" cell-style="solid" padding="12pt" colspan="30"><grid-item-label><icon src="https://iconscdn.pictographic.ai/image/6FXAuU2pLPf3ursjSwNq7P.svg?stroke=45" source="image.pictographic.icon" alt="soldiers joining one group"></icon></grid-item-label><h4 font-size="24pt">One army</h4><p font-size="17pt">Rebel soldiers joined the imperial army.</p></grid-item><grid-item id="Pdy8CHNi9a" class="panel" background-color="palette-8" cell-style="solid" padding="12pt" colspan="30"><grid-item-label><icon src="https://iconscdn.pictographic.ai/image/5SfBYQfhuwEpnROFgQ7S.svg?stroke=45" source="image.pictographic.icon" alt="local ballot and paid account"></icon></grid-item-label><h4 font-size="24pt">More local say</h4><p font-size="17pt">The south chose its next governor; the empire paid the republic's debts.</p></grid-item><grid-item id="LsOVcFud7L" class="panel" background-color="palette-7" cell-style="solid" padding="12pt" colspan="30"><grid-item-label><icon src="https://iconscdn.pictographic.ai/image/4q9aSLkkQiqUkA66t02l.svg?stroke=45" source="image.pictographic.icon" alt="import tax stamp twenty five percent"></icon></grid-item-label><h4 font-size="24pt">25% tax</h4><p font-size="17pt">Imported charque finally faced a 25% tax.</p></grid-item></grid></grid-item></grid><notes><p>Frame this as negotiation, not a glorious victory or crushing defeat. Source: <a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ragamuffin_War">Ragamuffin War overview</a>.</p></notes></section>
<section image-layout="blank" id="UGPoDNxAKp"><grid spacing="none"><grid-item id="0jNP2WfnTd"><h2 font-size="36pt">Why people still talk about it</h2><grid marker="icon" marker-size="small" marker-position="above" marker-align="start" spacing="medium" vertical-sizing="fill"><grid-item id="qNozMx75X7" class="coded code-character" background-color="palette-5" cell-style="solid" padding="14pt 16pt" colspan="15"><grid-item-label><icon src="https://iconscdn.pictographic.ai/image/Jwk3dgjBiUtQeQUuEStV.svg?stroke=45" source="image.pictographic.icon" alt="ten year calendar"></icon></grid-item-label><h3 font-size="21pt">10 years</h3><p font-size="17pt">Brazil's biggest and longest regional revolt.</p></grid-item><grid-item id="vnX7u_nZ6S" class="coded code-setting" background-color="palette-6" cell-style="solid" padding="14pt 16pt" colspan="15"><grid-item-label><icon src="https://iconscdn.pictographic.ai/image/dCHpKHGSHFAcYaB75V3W.svg?stroke=45" source="image.pictographic.icon" alt="annual celebration calendar date"></icon></grid-item-label><h3 font-size="21pt">20 September</h3><p font-size="17pt">Rio Grande do Sul still marks the date every year.</p></grid-item><grid-item id="uoydHqVoy6" class="coded code-resolution" background-color="palette-8" cell-style="solid" padding="14pt 16pt" colspan="15"><grid-item-label><icon src="https://iconscdn.pictographic.ai/image/mFiXglkNuAgHbRpa2lQ4.svg?stroke=45" source="image.pictographic.icon" alt="sailing ship traveling to Italy"></icon></grid-item-label><h3 font-size="21pt">Garibaldi sailed home</h3><p font-size="17pt">He later helped unite Italy.</p></grid-item><grid-item id="PBDLKJtIjN" class="coded code-problem" background-color="palette-7" cell-style="solid" padding="14pt 16pt" colspan="15"><grid-item-label><icon src="https://iconscdn.pictographic.ai/image/Wn7AhS2ngGpoW8sE6Irf.svg?stroke=45" source="image.pictographic.icon" alt="proud team badge"></icon></grid-item-label><h3 font-size="21pt">“Farroupilha”</h3><p font-size="17pt">An insult became a badge of pride.</p></grid-item></grid></grid-item></grid><notes><p>Sources: <a href="https://www.encyclopedia.com/humanities/encyclopedias-almanacs-transcripts-and-maps/farroupilha-revolt">Encyclopedia.com</a> and <a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ragamuffin_War">Ragamuffin War overview</a>.</p></notes></section>
<section image-layout="blank" id="sMXk7xmI_s"><grid spacing="none"><grid-item id="ayRdk1hMEf"><h2>Quiz time!</h2><grid direction="vertical" spacing="medium" vertical-sizing="fill"><grid-item id="5l-pBFCAZO"><grid marker="icon" marker-size="small" marker-position="inline" spacing="medium"><grid-item id="7BFbdqR9eT" class="panel" cell-style="subtle" padding="14pt 18pt" colspan="20"><grid-item-label><icon src="https://iconscdn.pictographic.ai/image/bI1NKwwyoF20IGvcZrab.svg?stroke=45" source="image.pictographic.icon" alt="salted dried beef strip"></icon></grid-item-label><p font-size="18pt"><b>What food started the whole argument?</b></p></grid-item><grid-item id="K4N8VMY7Ag" class="panel" cell-style="subtle" padding="14pt 18pt" colspan="20"><grid-item-label><icon src="https://iconscdn.pictographic.ai/image/9eg9RNQebKpKhCBhFg5bqe.svg?stroke=45" source="image.pictographic.icon" alt="torn cloth rag"></icon></grid-item-label><p font-size="18pt"><b>What does the word <i>farrapo</i> mean?</b></p></grid-item><grid-item id="33gE0XxbEy" class="panel" cell-style="subtle" padding="14pt 18pt" colspan="20"><grid-item-label><icon src="https://iconscdn.pictographic.ai/image/CdsdhEgYhJ80rcAjfc5A.svg?stroke=45" source="image.pictographic.icon" alt="young emperor crown"></icon></grid-item-label><p font-size="18pt"><b>How old was Emperor Pedro II when the war began?</b></p></grid-item></grid></grid-item><grid-item id="d82e_HvnEP"><grid marker="icon" marker-size="small" marker-position="inline" spacing="medium"><spacer span="5"></spacer><grid-item id="dRVHcZm0HD" class="panel" cell-style="subtle" padding="14pt 18pt" colspan="25"><grid-item-label><icon src="https://iconscdn.pictographic.ai/image/7X3JnWz1eCevkJQl5W6p.svg?stroke=45" source="image.pictographic.icon" alt="sailing boat on wheeled cart"></icon></grid-item-label><p font-size="18pt"><b>How did Garibaldi get his boats past the warships?</b></p></grid-item><grid-item id="v6_xArEhb2" class="panel" cell-style="subtle" padding="14pt 18pt" colspan="25"><grid-item-label><icon src="https://iconscdn.pictographic.ai/image/wndZTsG5F391xz62eT0s.svg?stroke=45" source="image.pictographic.icon" alt="calendar showing passing years"></icon></grid-item-label><p font-size="18pt"><b>How many years did the war last?</b></p></grid-item><spacer span="5"></spacer></grid></grid-item></grid></grid-item></grid><notes><p>Read one card at a time. Let children answer with a partner before moving to the answer slide.</p></notes></section>
<section image-layout="blank" id="3uJnD5vbw6"><grid spacing="none"><grid-item id="eOMzBbgJHF"><h2>Answers</h2><grid divider="sm neutral-border" marker="number" marker-style="solid" marker-shape="circle" marker-position="inline" direction="vertical" spacing="none" class="chip" style="--marker-inline-size: 42pt; --marker-gap: 18pt;"><grid-item id="FKoSQxeIj_" padding="12pt 0"><p font-size="21pt"><b>Charque</b>, salted dried beef.</p></grid-item><grid-item id="nF2Nob2olX" padding="12pt 0"><p font-size="21pt"><b>“Rag.”</b> The rebels turned the nickname into a badge of honour.</p></grid-item><grid-item id="XFikwqczsY" padding="12pt 0"><p font-size="21pt"><b>Nine years old.</b></p></grid-item><grid-item id="Z4csqx05p2" padding="12pt 0"><p font-size="21pt">He rolled the boats overland on <b>ox-drawn carts</b>.</p></grid-item><grid-item id="9BIgjH7GkV" padding="12pt 0"><p font-size="21pt"><b>Ten years:</b> 1835 to 1845.</p></grid-item></grid></grid-item></grid><notes><p>Check each answer against the matching question card. Finish by asking which fact was the most surprising.</p></notes></section>